.Dd June 16, 2026
.Dt QSTAR-LUA 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qstar-lua
.Nd QStar authoring file format
.Sh DESCRIPTION
QStar authoring files are sandboxed Lua 5.4 files that construct a deterministic
build graph.
The root file is
.Pa qstar.lua .
Subdirectory fragments are named
.Pa <folder>.qst .
Helper modules are named
.Pa <folder>/<folder>.qsm .
.Pp
The QStar 1.0 compatibility policy lives in
.Pa docs/qstar-compatibility-policy.md .
Consumer-facing project, target, generated artifact, command, stage, run target,
and GLP activation syntax are stable-at-v1 candidates. Provider-author APIs,
daemon protocol details, optional real-compiler validation lanes, performance
snapshots, and internal debug state remain beta or report-only unless promoted
by that policy.
For GLP, Q257 keeps the consumer surface as a v1 stable candidate while
classifying the provider-author API as a versioned beta contract.
.Pp
The main entrypoints are:
.Bl -tag -width "qstar.custom_target"
.It Ic qstar.project
Project metadata, including name, version, root, build_dir, generated_dir, and
compile_commands.
The command-line
.Fl B
option overrides build_dir for the current invocation.
The generated_dir field controls the package-relative root for generated
outputs and defaults to
.Pa generated .
.It Ic qstar.option
Declare a typed project build option that can be overridden before graph
evaluation with global CLI
.Fl D Ar name=value
or
.Fl D Ns Ar name=value .
The supported fields are
.Ic type ,
.Ic value ,
.Ic choices ,
and
.Ic description .
Supported types are
.Li string ,
.Li boolean ,
.Li integer ,
.Li combo ,
and
.Li list .
The call returns the effective Lua value, so projects branch with ordinary Lua
.Ic if
and write explicit compiler or linker argv through configs and target fields.
.Nm
does not infer target triples, architectures, boards, runtimes, or toolchain
policy from option names.
.It Ic qstar.variant
Declare a named read-only user metadata table. Built-in fields are only the
name argument,
.Ic values ,
.Ic description ,
and
.Ic tags .
Keys such as
.Ic arch ,
.Ic triple ,
.Ic cpu ,
.Ic board ,
.Ic mode ,
or
.Ic runtime
are project metadata only when they appear under
.Ic values ;
they are not parsed by
.Nm
and do not inject argv.
.It Ic qstar.toolset
Explicit compiler, archive, link, response-file, and external tool role bundle.
.It Ic qstar.use_language
Activate a bundled or project-local language provider. The short form
.Ic qstar.use_language("zig")
first checks
.Pa qstar/languages/zig/zig.qsm
and then falls back to the installed standard provider bundle at
.Pa share/qstar/languages/zig/zig.qsm ;
the bundled standard provider set currently includes
.Li zig ,
.Li rust ,
and
.Li cuda ;
the folder form
.Ic qstar.use_language("qstar/languages/zig")
loads
.Pa qstar/languages/zig/zig.qsm .
Calling
.Ic qstar.use_language
again for the same manifest returns the cached provider helper table, so root
files and workspace fragments can reuse the same provider. A different
manifest that declares an already active namespace remains an error.
The returned provider table may expose helper functions such as
.Ic zig.tools
or
.Ic zig.options .
Provider-declared
.Ic options
schemas validate dynamic
.Ic lang.<namespace>
tables, including string, bool, list, enum, and default metadata.
Provider-declared source unit suffixes are registered with the graph-level
source registry, so an activated provider can classify raw source strings such as
.Pa src/main.zig
into provider-owned object actions.
Explicit provider helpers remain useful for source-local options or suffix
collision disambiguation.
.It Ic qstar.language_provider
Declare a provider manifest. This provider-author API is beta and is valid only
inside provider
.Pa .qsm
manifests, must use
.Li api = "qstar.lang/1" ,
and names the restricted
.Pa provider.lua
implementation through the
.Ic implementation
field.
The optional
.Ic scaffold
field declares validated init metadata with
.Li api = "qstar.scaffold/1" .
When a primary provider shape is available,
.Ic qstar init
materializes its files, targets, fragments, default tools, and default
options. Scaffold file and fragment paths must be package-relative; command,
script, fetch, network, and absolute-path surfaces are not part of the schema.
Future provider manifest versions are rejected instead of guessed; a manifest
that does not use
.Li qstar.lang/1
fails with the language-provider API diagnostic.
.It Ic qstar.config
Reusable target option bundle referenced by target
.Ic configs
lists.
.It Ic qstar.executable
Executable target.
.It Ic qstar.staticlib
Static library target.
.It Ic qstar.sharedlib
Shared library target. macOS platform context produces
.Pa lib<name>.dylib
with an
.Ar @rpath
install name, and Linux platform context produces
.Pa lib<name>.so
with a soname. Consumers that link a QStar shared library receive a build-tree
runtime search path based on
.Ar @loader_path
on macOS or
.Ar $ORIGIN
on Linux. Windows platform context produces a primary runtime
.Pa .dll
artifact and a secondary import
.Pa .lib
artifact. Dependents link against the import library, while
.Ic qstar.target_file(label)
selects the runtime DLL by default and
.Ic qstar.target_file(label, { artifact = "import_lib" })
selects the import library. PDB/debug artifact ownership remains deferred.
.It Ic qstar.objectlib
Object collection target. It compiles or collects object inputs but does not
produce an archive, shared library, executable, or primary artifact.
Artifact-producing targets consume it through their
.Ic objects
field. Calling
.Ic qstar.target_file(...)
for an object library is an error. The implemented compile context is
.Li own
or
.Li consumer .
.Li own
compiles once under the object library's configs, language options, and toolset.
.Li consumer
keeps source ownership in the object library but compiles each source under the
consuming artifact target's effective configs, language options, and toolset,
using per-consumer object identities. Object libraries accept built-in
C/C++/ASM sources, activated GLP raw source strings, generated object outputs,
and explicit provider source tokens in
.Li own
context. Explicit provider source tokens already carry a concrete
action/output and are rejected in
.Li consumer
context; use raw provider source strings or
.Li own
context instead.
.It Ic qstar.interface
Artifact-free typed dependency target. Fields are
.Ic deps ,
.Ic public_deps ,
.Ic private_deps ,
.Ic visibility ,
.Ic compile_usage ,
and
.Ic link_usage .
Usage tables accept only
.Ic options
and
.Ic inputs .
Options are appended verbatim to consumer compile or link argv vectors, while
inputs are rebuild dependencies and do not become argv items. Public dependency
usage propagates transitively; private dependency usage does not propagate past
its owner.
.It Ic qstar.imported
Package-local prebuilt artifact target. The
.Ic artifacts
field maps
.Li default , darwin , linux , windows , generic
to artifact lists containing
.Ic id , role , path , primary .
The current platform entry wins and
.Li default
is the fallback. Exactly one artifact is primary. The
.Li link
role selects the implementation artifact used by link consumers. The optional
.Ic artifact_kind
value is descriptive metadata only; QStar never infers compiler or linker flags
from it, an artifact id, or a filename suffix.
.It Ic qstar.tool
Declare a package-local executable tool path with optional visibility.
.Ic qstar.tool_file(label)
references this path. The same helper accepts an imported artifact with
.Li role = "tool"
or a QStar executable/test target. Built executable tools create a producer edge
before the consuming generated action in both Stella and Ninja.
.It Ic qstar.test
Test executable target.
.Pp
Artifact targets and configs split
.Ic link_options
from
.Ic link_inputs .
.Ic link_options
items are appended to the link argv exactly as authored.
.Ic link_inputs
tracks package-relative files or
.Ic qstar.target_file(...)
artifacts as link action rebuild inputs without adding argv items.
Artifact targets may also declare
.Ic compile_usage
and
.Ic link_usage
for explicit consumer requirements. Existing
.Ic deps , public_deps , private_deps , libs , lib_dirs , link_options
and
.Ic link_inputs
remain supported.
macOS frameworks are not a generic top-level target field; write them inside a
Darwin-specific branch as
.Ic link.frameworks .
.It Ic qstar.custom_target
Generated action using a
.Ic qstar.cli
argv vector. Fields are
.Ic inputs ,
.Ic outputs ,
.Ic command ,
.Ic description ,
and optional
.Ic toolset .
When
.Ic toolset
is present, bare PATH command tools must be declared by that toolset's
.Ic path_tools .
.It Ic qstar.transform
Single-input single-output generated artifact transform sugar. It lowers to the
same generated action contract as
.Ic qstar.custom_target
and accepts the same
.Ic toolset
and
.Ic description
policy fields.
.It Ic qstar.configure_file
Deterministic configured file or config header generator using
.Ic qstar.output .
.It Ic qstar.run_target
External command with first-class inputs, timeout, and optional expect checks.
The
.Ic inputs
field accepts package-relative files,
.Ic qstar.target_file(...)
artifacts, and
.Ic qstar.stage_dir(...)
layout-root tokens. Inside
.Ic command = qstar.cli { ... } ,
.Ic qstar.input(N)
resolves to the Nth run input.
.It Ic qstar.group
Deps-only aggregate target with no command, artifact, install output, or
.Ic qstar.target_file
artifact.
.It Ic qstar.import_file
Evaluate a package-relative
.Pa .qst
graph fragment exactly once.
.It Ic qstar.import_module
Evaluate a package-relative module folder as
.Pa <name>/<name>.qsm
and return its cached read-only export table.
.It Ic qstar.subdir
Evaluate the canonical subdirectory fragment
.Pa <dir>/<basename>.qst .
.It Ic qstar.target_family
Declare a lint grouping primitive for shared-source variants.
.It Ic qstar.command
Declare a root
.Pa qstar.lua
project command. Project commands are forbidden in
.Pa .qst
fragments,
.Pa .qsm
modules, and provider files. Supported fields are
.Ic description ,
.Ic options ,
.Ic env ,
.Ic working_dir ,
.Ic steps ,
.Ic is_default ,
.Ic hidden ,
and
.Ic aliases .
Command names and aliases cannot collide with built-in
.Nm
CLI commands.
The name
.Ic install
is not a built-in CLI command in the QStar DSL surface; projects may define it
as a normal
.Ic qstar.command
when they want a user-facing layout export workflow.
.It Ic qstar.command_spec
Create a pure, deeply read-only project command specification with the same
fields, typed options, and steps as
.Ic qstar.command .
This helper does not mutate the graph and may be used by an ordinary
.Pa .qsm
module. The value contains deterministic scalar and table data only.
.It Ic qstar.command_set
Materialize one non-empty contiguous list of
.Ic qstar.command_spec
values as ordinary project commands. This API is allowed only in root
.Pa qstar.lua ;
plain tables are rejected. Materialized commands share direct-command name,
alias, default, call-cycle, dispatch, and
.Ic qstar commands --format json
semantics.
.It Ic qstar.step.build
Project command step that builds a target, generated action, stage, run target,
or group label.
.It Ic qstar.step.test
Project command step that runs a
.Ic qstar.test
target selection.
.It Ic qstar.step.stage
Project command step that materializes a
.Ic qstar.stage
layout. The optional table supports
.Ic root
and
.Ic dry_run .
.It Ic qstar.step.check
Project command step that validates the graph or the selected label.
.It Ic qstar.step.lint
Project command step that runs authoring lint.
.It Ic qstar.step.run
Project command step that executes a command-local argv-vector action. The table
requires
.Ic command = qstar.cli { ... }
and may include
.Ic inputs ,
.Ic working_dir ,
.Ic description ,
.Ic env ,
.Ic timeout ,
.Ic expect ,
and
.Ic when .
Inputs accept package-relative files,
.Ic qstar.target_file(...) ,
and
.Ic qstar.stage_dir(...) .
.Ic qstar.input(N)
inside the command resolves to the Nth input. Output is captured under
.Pa build/qstar/logs ,
timeouts and expect failures write replay metadata, and action logs are
available as
.Ic qstar-command:<name>:run:<index> .
.It Ic qstar.step.call
Project command step that calls another project command or alias. Cycles are
errors.
.It Ic qstar.step.export_stage
Project command step that materializes a
.Ic qstar.stage
layout and copies it to
.Ic to .
The destination must be package-relative and may be a
.Ic qstar.param("path_option")
reference.
.It Ic qstar.param.string Ns , Ic qstar.param.path Ns , Ic qstar.param.bool Ns , Ic qstar.param.int Ns , Ic qstar.param.enum Ns , Ic qstar.param.list
Declare typed project command option schemas. Common fields are
.Ic description ,
.Ic required ,
.Ic default ,
and enum
.Ic choices .
Command-line option values are validated at dispatch. Bool options accept
.Fl -flag ,
.Fl -flag=true ,
.Fl -flag=false ,
and
.Fl -no-flag .
.Ic qstar.param("name")
references a runtime option value inside
.Ic qstar.cli .
.Ic qstar.arg_if(qstar.param("flag"), arg)
and
.Ic qstar.args_if(qstar.param("flag"), args)
conditionally append argv items when the referenced bool option is true. Step
.Ic when
fields also require a bool option reference.
.It Ic qstar.cli
Declare an argv-vector command. Shell strings are not accepted.
.It Ic qstar.status
Declare a validated one-line CMake-style build status description for
user-defined actions.
.It Ic qstar.input
Reference a custom target or run target input by index inside a
.Ic qstar.cli
argv vector.
.It Ic qstar.output
Declare or reference a generated output path. Output paths must stay under the
effective
.Ic generated_dir .
The metadata form
.Ic qstar.output(path, {format = "object"})
marks a generated
.Pa .o
or
.Pa .obj
as an object artifact. Such outputs may be listed in target
.Ic sources
and are consumed directly by archive or link actions instead of being compiled
again. This is the supported bridge for external languages such as Objective-C,
Rust, Zig, or Swift when a package-local wrapper or allowlisted tool produces an
object file; QStar does not parse or own those language semantics.
.It Ic qstar.target_file
Reference the artifact produced by a target or generated action. It cannot
reference a
.Ic qstar.group
because group targets have no artifact. The optional selector form
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qstar.target_file("//:plugin", { artifact = "import_lib" })
.Ed
addresses a named secondary artifact. Q223 uses this for the Windows shared
library import
.Pa .lib
artifact while the default form still resolves to the primary runtime
.Pa .dll .
.It Ic qstar.tool_file
Reference the executable artifact of a typed tool dependency. Accepted targets
are
.Ic qstar.tool ,
an imported artifact with
.Li role = "tool" ,
.Ic qstar.executable ,
or
.Ic qstar.test .
When used as the first item of
.Ic qstar.cli
for a generated action, the referenced executable target is built first and its
resolved path becomes argv[0].
.It Ic qstar.stage_dir
Reference the layout root produced by a
.Ic qstar.stage
rule. Use it in
.Ic run_target.inputs
and pass it to argv with
.Ic qstar.input(N)
so the stage root is tracked as an action input.
Stella and Ninja both build the stage producer and use its manifest as the
dependency marker before running the consuming action.
.It Ic qstar.stage_file
Map a source artifact or source file into a
.Ic qstar.stage
tree.
.It Ic qstar.files
Declare a literal file list.
.It Ic qstar.join
Join path segments as a slash-separated package-relative string. Use
.Ic qstar.append
for list composition.
.It Ic qstar.copy
Deep-copy an authoring table.
.It Ic qstar.append
Return a new list with values or list items appended.
.It Ic qstar.merge
Return a deep-merged plain table. List fields append.
.It Ic qstar.extend
Deep-merge overlays into a base plain table and return the base table.
.It Ic qstar.stage
Copy-only package or staging tree.
.El
.Pp
Language-specific options must live under
.Ic lang.<namespace> .
Built-in namespaces are
.Ic lang.c ,
.Ic lang.cxx ,
and
.Ic lang.asm ;
activated language providers add dynamic namespaces such as
.Ic lang.zig
according to the provider option schema. Top-level include/header/module/compile
fields are rejected.
.Pp
Target
.Ic configs
are applied in list order. List fields append, target-local list fields append
last, and target-local scalar fields override scalar values from configs.
Configs must be evaluated before targets that reference them.
Configs cannot create sources, deps, commands, outputs, stages, or installable
artifacts.
.Sh LUA SUBSET
Allowed helper features include
.Ic local function ,
local variables, table literals,
.Ic ipairs ,
.Ic pairs ,
.Ic table.insert ,
and safe
.Ic string.*
helpers.
Global assignment, filesystem/process/network APIs, dynamic loading, and debug
interfaces are forbidden.
Lua
.Ic require
is forbidden; use
.Ic qstar.import_module
for helper modules.
Makefile-style
.Ic $VAR
string expansion is not performed; use Lua local values and QStar authoring
helpers instead.
.Pp
.Pa .qsm
modules must return a table and cannot declare graph nodes such as targets,
configs, toolsets, project metadata, stages, or subdirs.
Repeated
.Ic qstar.import_module
calls for the same canonical module entry reuse the cached exports instead of
re-evaluating the file.
They may return values built with
.Ic qstar.status
for use in description fields.
.Pp
.Ic description
fields on
.Ic qstar.custom_target ,
.Ic qstar.configure_file ,
.Ic qstar.run_target ,
and
.Ic qstar.stage
must be written as
.Ic qstar.status Ns Pq Ar text .
Empty strings, newlines, and text longer than 240 bytes are rejected.
The same description is used by Stella progress output, Ninja
.Li description =
lowering, the
.Ic action-log
CLI, replay output, and last-failure metadata.
The QStar LSP resolves definitions on
.Ic qstar.import_file
strings to
.Pa .qst
files and definitions on
.Ic qstar.import_module
strings to the corresponding
.Pa <name>/<name>.qsm
module entry. Definitions on
.Ic qstar.use_language
strings resolve to the provider manifest
.Pa qstar/languages/<id>/<id>.qsm
or the explicit provider folder form. At runtime, short ids also fall back to
the installed standard provider bundle under
.Pa share/qstar/languages .
The manifest is validated with
.Ic qstar.language_provider ,
then its
.Pa provider.lua
implementation is loaded in a restricted provider sandbox and only manifest
.Ic exports
are returned to user code. Provider
.Ic options
schemas validate dynamic
.Ic lang.<namespace>
tables. Provider
.Ic scaffold
metadata validates optional project-shape files, targets, fragments, default
tools, and default options consumed by
.Ic qstar init
when that provider is the primary init language. Provider implementations build lowered action argv vectors with
.Ic qstar.argv
inside the restricted provider sandbox.
The author-facing manifest fields
.Ic id ,
.Ic version ,
.Ic namespace ,
.Ic implementation ,
.Ic tools ,
.Ic units ,
.Ic finals ,
.Ic options ,
.Ic exports ,
and
.Ic scaffold ,
plus lowered action result fields
.Ic command ,
.Ic env ,
.Ic inputs ,
.Ic outputs ,
and
.Ic depfile ,
are documented in
.Pa docs/language-provider-backend-contract.md
but remain beta until the provider-author contract is frozen or versioned.
The bundled
.Li zig ,
.Li rust ,
and
.Li cuda
provider ids, namespaces, documented helper exports, documented options, source
classification behavior, and init vendoring behavior are consumer-facing stable
candidates; their implementation details remain beta.
.Sh DECLARATION SCHEMAS
Every public declaration table has an exact field and Lua type schema.
Unknown fields, wrong types, and list tables with named, sparse, or non-integer
keys are rejected during graph evaluation. Diagnostics include the Lua source
file and line, public API name, and declaration label. Artifact targets,
object libraries, groups, and run targets use separate schemas so fields that
have no lowering meaning cannot be silently retained.
.Pp
Keys under
.Ic qstar.variant.values
remain user-defined metadata. Ordinary Lua tables returned by
.Ic qstar.import_module
are not declaration tables. Activated provider options under
.Ic lang.<namespace>
are validated by that provider's dynamic option schema rather than a core
allowlist. The complete contract is documented in
.Pa share/doc/qstar/docs/public-declaration-schemas.md
and
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/reference/declaration-schemas.md .
.Sh CONSTANTS
.Nm
provides constants such as
.Ic QSTAR_VERSION ,
.Ic QSTAR_HOST_OS ,
.Ic QSTAR_HOST_ARCH ,
.Ic QSTAR_PACKAGE_ROOT ,
.Ic QSTAR_PROJECT_ROOT .
Namespace forms include
.Ic qstar.version ,
.Ic qstar.host.os ,
.Ic qstar.host.arch ,
and
.Ic qstar.project.root .
.Ic qstar.host
is read-only.
Host-specific authoring uses ordinary Lua
.Ic if
statements over
.Ic qstar.host.os
and
.Ic qstar.host.arch ;
QStar does not expose a built-in OS or architecture condition-object grammar.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qstar 1 ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/reference/qstar-lua.md ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/reference/object-artifacts.md ,
.Pa share/doc/qstar/wiki/reference/configs.md ,
